<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Breaking news from AFRICA, Maghreb and Sub-Saharan Africa - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of events, politics and social issues across Africa, including North Africa (the Maghreb) and the Sahel, aided by our network of correspondents and experts across the continent.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:22:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Kabila launches new coalition with M23</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:587d1678b2ae203d06a715eace8fb45cdee95db05c1c7d0a5439b041f6ff9503</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:22:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:21:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kabila-launches-new-coalition-with-m23--ed60166777a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kabila-launches-new-coalition-with-m23" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Joseph Kabila has been named leader of a new rebel coalition, vowing to topple the government. Also, Africa's largest ever IPO has been extended. And Formula ⁠1 ⁠will return to ⁠Africa in ​the early 2030s, once a new circuit is built in Rwanda.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>In Kenya, recycled plastic gets a second life as chess pieces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9b314f10a719465175407b02e260e801a0925eba152efa945797be8b3b34b73</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:28:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/in-kenya-recycled-plastic-gets-a-second-life-as-chess-pieces--70350efdf983.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/in-kenya-recycled-plastic-gets-a-second-life-as-chess-pieces" /><summary type="html">In Nairobi, a project is helping children develop focus, patience and critical thinking through chess, using pieces made from recycled plastic waste.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africa suspends asylum applications amid renewed anti-immigrant protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b11503837c4748cc6a105af2aecb385f4e5ba95ea293b5fcf1e90db4195bc42b</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:15:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-amid-renewed-anti-immigrant-protests--0599fa64feef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-amid-renewed-anti-immigrant-protests" /><summary type="html">Tensions have flared in South Africa after a court ruling prompted the government to open its application system to all foreign nationals, regardless of their legal status. Despite applications remaining subject to approval, anti-immigrant protests erupted outside several Home Affairs offices, forcing authorities to temporarily suspend refugee and asylum applications. FRANCE 24's Eunice Masson has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian forces enter key Tigray town, raising fears among residents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0541092e325bfbc3bb16c3242091cb0c4c455ea8a61a7ee208a975575b1e67df</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:13:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-raising-fears-among-residents--da75969b90c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-raising-fears-among-residents" /><summary type="html">Ethiopian federal forces and their allies have entered a key town in northern Tigray near the Eritrean border after rebel fighters withdrew. As the conflict intensifies, residents fear further violence and instability. Tom Canetti has the latest from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: Social media becomes a battleground for propaganda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b405ddfde06e35018e596a6a30109038e5e62ce04086b34e9ea881cce6e137f2</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T10:00:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-social-media-becomes-a-battleground-for-propaganda--7bc0eed62661.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-social-media-becomes-a-battleground-for-propaganda" /><summary type="html">Millions of Ethiopians rely on social media for daily news. But as fighting resumes in the country’s north between federal forces and a coalition of rebel groups, these platforms have become a breeding ground for propaganda and disinformation. Pro-government and pro-rebel accounts are battling to shape the news, while journalists’ limited access to the front lines makes it increasingly difficult to verify what is happening on the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tunisian duo Jathb blends Sufi traditions with electronic music</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd0c9a3af1abd79d35fa660038f1100659b9115c578b733a0b599411c1439f68</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T09:59:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tunisian-duo-jathb-blends-sufi-traditions-with-electronic-music--06b68a7b515e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tunisian-duo-jathb-blends-sufi-traditions-with-electronic-music" /><summary type="html">Tunisian musical duo Jathb is reviving traditional Sufi chants by blending them with electronic beats and therapeutic sounds. After four years of gaining recognition both in Tunisia and internationally, the duo is also working to preserve the centuries-old Sufi music and texts that form part of the country’s cultural heritage.</summary></entry><entry><title>DR Congo’s former president Kabila to lead new movement with M23 rebels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c626a2e7bc11eb684b9ed86c54bd9b7f6d589f477f18a3dbfbe37eefb67218b4</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T21:27:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261012-dr-congo-former-president-joseph-kabila-to-lead-new-movement-with-m23-rebels--d5bb01da2cbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261012-dr-congo-former-president-joseph-kabila-to-lead-new-movement-with-m23-rebels" /><summary type="html">Former DR Congo president Joseph Kabila announced a new political-military alliance with Rwanda-backed M23 rebels on Monday, despite being sentenced to death in absentia for alleged complicity with the group. The move comes as debate grows over constitutional changes ahead of President Felix Tshisekedi’s final term ending in 2028.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian government forces enter key Tigray town near Eritrea border</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71902af3017a53c58920b69fe3eb8249db265ce86a6def0705d11d2da93a24e0</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T20:34:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-govt-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-near-eritrea-border--b8ceaad00564.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-govt-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-near-eritrea-border" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Ethiopian forces tighten their grip on Tigray, advancing into the key town of Adwa after rebels withdrew. Also, police arrest 30 people amid violence across South Africa. Plus we head to Tunisia, where ancient Sufi chants collide with pulsating electronic beats.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>At least 139 migrants die in boat wreck between Djibouti and Yemen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94f3e030076d631ad949b4f1a160a2f5c345ffbd406613050ef2654e90af3248</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:24:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/at-least-139-migrants-die-in-boat-wreck-between-djibouti-and-yemen--b289888d8821.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/at-least-139-migrants-die-in-boat-wreck-between-djibouti-and-yemen" /><summary type="html">At least 139 migrants died, including 15 children and 84 went missing when an overcrowded boat sank on its way from Djibouti to Yemen on the night between October 8 and 9. The International Organization for Migration said most of the people were Ethiopian when the vessel capsized off north of the town of Obock. Details by Morgan Ayre.</summary></entry><entry><title>Scores of gold miners killed in air strikes on Egypt-Sudan border, rights group says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95980ca26a969995e3a6e643da8bd370ea3a15a757cbeaf8beefd1bc12e84537</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T01:28:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261012-egypt-sudan-border-airstrikes-gold-miners-killed--da77bc6ac540.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261012-egypt-sudan-border-airstrikes-gold-miners-killed" /><summary type="html">At least 72 workers were killed in air strikes on a gold mine on the Sudan-Egypt border on Saturday, a Sudanese rights group said on Sunday. The Emergency Lawyers organisation accused Egypt’s air force of the attack. AFP could not independently verify the account and Egypt has issued no official comment.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>At least 139 migrants dead, more than 84 missing after boat capsizes off Djibouti</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b62fa0bce66971a96b0702caa92ed3df040487db33d4420cd6e1cf8be9905cd</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T09:24:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261011-at-least-hundred-migrants-dead-scores-missing-after-boat-capsizes-off-djibouti--63d1cd578d0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261011-at-least-hundred-migrants-dead-scores-missing-after-boat-capsizes-off-djibouti" /><summary type="html">At least 139 migrants, including at least 15 children, died and 84 remain missing after a boat carrying 350 people capsized off Djibouti en route to Yemen, the International Organisation for Migration said on Sunday.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>South African judge Navi Pillay awarded Nobel Peace Prize</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55b79859e112c8adc8f3bae6ea5cace5f78c8c9fe1f74c17a46af217ba5bddf7</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T21:53:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/south-african-judge-awarded-nobel-peace-prize--abdd3a99d080.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-african-judge-awarded-nobel-peace-prize" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: South African judge and human rights champion Navi Pillay has been awarded the Nobel Peace Prize. Also, in Kenya, health officials in Nairobi are still racing to track dozens of people linked to the man who died from Ebola earlier this week. Finally, Moroccan-British photographer Hassan Hajjaj has built a global reputation with his vibrant portraits, and 40 of his iconic "Rock Stars" are currently taking centre stage in Paris.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Sierra Leone: From 'blood diamonds' to stones of hope?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c18fb58e442e36f389b64c529efd388723f06f81a348b82f66884e6e1f13a9df</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:58:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261009-sierra-leone-from-blood-diamonds-to-stones-of-hopen--522d29c385dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261009-sierra-leone-from-blood-diamonds-to-stones-of-hopen" /><summary type="html">"Blood diamonds" became infamous for funding the brutal civil war in Sierra Leone. Beginning 25 years ago, the Kimberley Process aimed to put an end to this illegal trade. Accused of complicity in the conflict, the diamond industry has since sought to clean up its image, emphasising an ethical shift. But a quarter of a century on, have the former "blood diamonds" truly become synonymous with development? FRANCE 24's Sarah Sakho, Simon Martin and Saidu Bah report.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>Foreign aid to Africa falls by over 25%: How women and children are bearing the brunt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40f988a63c93b2c6732e4c0048334aed9c228f98f6211b5ba083d24486da9f3a</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T12:22:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261009-foreign-aid-to-africa-falls-by-over-25-how-women-and-children-are-bearing-the-brunt--1838f18aba87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261009-foreign-aid-to-africa-falls-by-over-25-how-women-and-children-are-bearing-the-brunt" /><summary type="html">As international aid to Africa dries up, what does it mean for women and children on the ground? We report from Kenya on the impact of cuts to US-aid backed health programmes for women. Annette Young also talks to Nana Zulu from the African Women's Development Fund on what it means for the region as a whole. Plus the bravery of Borneo's female firefighters; as Indonesia endures its worst fire season in 11 years, these women are also facing a sexist backlash.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Eritrea and Ethiopia accuse each other of provoking war as Tigray rebels retreat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:788b3a4ee5a3dbd94fb79b8be1f2c3357c1d44ae65ef258bf018bd63b8338487</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T11:36:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261009-eritrea-ethiopia-accuse-each-other-of-provoking-war-as-tigray-rebels-retreat--2e14bf93030c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261009-eritrea-ethiopia-accuse-each-other-of-provoking-war-as-tigray-rebels-retreat" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia and Eritrea on Friday accused each other of starting a "war of agresson" days after the two countries severed diplomatic ties. Ethiopian officals estimate that up to 8,000 Eritrean soldiers are present in Tigray supporting rebels who last month launched attacks against federal forces.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Court of Arbitration for Sport hears Senegal's appeal over AFCON title</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25cf525af1d64901213e505c68a1d6e73f9c4f4607d518c45218d560e7c345fa</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T10:48:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261009-court-of-arbitration-for-sport-hears-senegal-s-appeal-over-afcon-title--d066765ef694.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261009-court-of-arbitration-for-sport-hears-senegal-s-appeal-over-afcon-title" /><summary type="html">Ten months after the explosive AFCON final, Senegal and Morocco are still fighting over the title, this time at sport's highest court. A verdict on Senegal's appeal against Morocco's victory by default is expected within days. Also, it's a race against time in Kenya. Health officials are tracing dozens of contacts after an Ebola patient died following a journey from DR Congo. Plus Zimbabwean author Simbarashe Steyn Kundizeza wins the 2026 Caine Prize for African Writing for his short story "The Blue Fighter".</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal and Morocco set for AFCON title rematch – in Swiss sports court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f08d32326d133b3517b7bc2d20afda5fae2b6500e3230bcccc0ec1e2dd486964</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T07:17:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261008-senegal-and-morocco-set-for-afcon-title-rematch-_-swiss-sports-court--c97e824c88b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261008-senegal-and-morocco-set-for-afcon-title-rematch-%E2%80%93-swiss-sports-court" /><summary type="html">Senegal and Morocco on Thursday are again set to fight for the African Cup of Nations title – this time, in the Court of Arbitration for Sport in Switzerland. The closed-door hearing comes nine months after the Confederation of African Football stripped Senegal of their trophy after the team's players walked off the pitch to protest a penalty during the chaotic final roughly nine months ago.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Africa joins the data centre backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2d8165488f9a9480169de783f538dff2ebbb430eae90bb3258dfe49057220f3</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T20:37:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa-joins-the-data-center-backlash--51a3f7ecc1aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa-joins-the-data-center-backlash" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Witnesses say Eritrean troops have moved into Ethiopia's Tigray region, but Asmara rejects the reports. Also, the African Union launches the Africa Credit Rating Agency, aiming to assess the financial health of African states and companies. Plus South African civil society is pushing back against the expansion of data centres that require vast amounts of electricity, water and land.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya reports its first-ever Ebola death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:749c8df01a6458136cf7ce164083f90b8912bcd30532760d49a62f723a169dbc</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T21:28:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death--a10b33fbf6f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Kenya records its first Ebola death after a man travelled there from the DR Congo via Uganda. Also, Comoros is tightening its rules on who can do business. And in South Africa, concerns are growing that xenophobia and hostility toward foreign nationals could be driving African tourists away.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya reports first-ever Ebola death after patient returns from DR Congo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c858737a8c86af14c196513bfd8e032c4cf759b431cb84d7cb286a280ef78aac</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T15:41:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261006-kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death-after-patient-returns-from-dr-congo--ad7202bd54ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261006-kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death-after-patient-returns-from-dr-congo" /><summary type="html">Kenya on Tuesday reported its first-ever Ebola death after a Kenyan national who had been living in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DR Congo) died after returning to the country. Kenya is the fourth country to record an Ebola case in the current outbreak, which was declared in eastern DR Congo in mid-May.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia again demands access to the Red Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59f6cc42a667c389ab59961de23032112ccd9e9ba68f3cff6a16bb10cafa9d43</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T20:28:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-again-demands-access-to-the-red-sea--806dbf10a5ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-again-demands-access-to-the-red-sea" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Ethiopia's leader Abiy Ahmed secures another term in office, but his country is sliding back into conflict. Also, several major cities across Senegal are battered by torrential rains. Plus some of the migrants being deported from the US fear being sent to African countries criminalising homosexuality.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Rwandan genocide suspect 'hunter' Dafroza Gauthier dies at 72</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06a75bd2eb354d7f928e0282b359eac105b94720ca38d8f52309d6154b5f2cf0</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T12:12:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261004-rwandan-genocide-hunter-dafroza-gauthier-dies-at-72--4acbb8946f0b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261004-rwandan-genocide-hunter-dafroza-gauthier-dies-at-72" /><summary type="html">For nearly 30 years, Dafroza Gauthier, along with her husband Alain, tracked down Rwandan refugees in France suspected of having participated in the Tutsi genocide. She died in Reims on Saturday after dedicating her life to bringing to justice those allegedly responsible for the 1994 massacre of more than 800,000 people.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian federal forces control Tigray capital as regional rivals meet in Egypt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69fd0f119879625a9d6ef591b3534faed1f5536d174f231fa50618427ae106df</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T10:22:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261004-ethiopian-federal-forces-control-tigray-capital-as-regional-rivals-meet-in-egypt--ec257ed5cbcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261004-ethiopian-federal-forces-control-tigray-capital-as-regional-rivals-meet-in-egypt" /><summary type="html">Troops loyal to Ethiopia's federal government were patrolling the streets of Mekelle on Sunday, a day after the Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF) withdrew its forces from the northern city. The government advance came as Ethiopia's regional rivals including Eritrea and Sudan met in the Egyptian coastal city of El-Alamein, calling for regional disputes to be settled through "peaceful means".</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's Tigray rebels abandon regional capital Mekelle as government forces enter city</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1db7a4072e5e2bc1563fbe48e54e23255e840fb0ba59f41818f798129e914738</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T07:58:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261003-ethiopia-s-tigray-rebels-abandon-regional-capital-of-mekelle-as-pro-government-forces-advan--a3cb00a5f7af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261003-ethiopia-s-tigray-rebels-abandon-regional-capital-of-mekelle-as-pro-government-forces-advance" /><summary type="html">Ethiopian federal forces have entered the capital of the northern Tigray region and seized its airport, witnesses said Saturday, reversing a takeover by rebels from the Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF) that prompted the suspension of commercial flights last month. The TPLF has been fighting against pro-government forces since September 23, raising fears of an all-out civil war similar to that of 2020-2022.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian army pushes back Tigrayan rebels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2778e3247a4ab8b6b4e296e96fb58a0f9176b274de3e7869343c569f0117f5bf</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T20:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261002-ethiopian-army-pushes-back-tigrayan-rebels--c1af64eb04a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261002-ethiopian-army-pushes-back-tigrayan-rebels" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia and Eritrea have severed ties and with tensions spreading across the region, the African Union is urging all sides to show restraint. Meanwhile, Ethiopia's army is advancing toward the Tigrayan capital as fighting intensifies and new explosions rock Addis Ababa.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>On the run for 20 years, Ugandan warlord Kony still 'active' within the Lord's Resistance Army</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc988266a79cafb04958478dca7e37b51c22b4b6e966f23d79818315685ab679</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T19:31:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261002-on-the-run-for-20-years-ugandan-warlord-kony-still-active-within-the-lord-s-resistance-army--aeeee67f194b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261002-on-the-run-for-20-years-ugandan-warlord-kony-still-active-within-the-lord-s-resistance-army" /><summary type="html">In recent months, the eastern Central African Republic has been hit by several attacks attributed to the Lord’s Resistance Army (LRA), a Ugandan militia infamous for its massacres and mass abductions of children in the 1990s and 2000s. The group's leader, Joseph Kony, wanted by the International Criminal Court for more than 20 years, remains at large. FRANCE 24 spoke to Leonie von Braun, the ICC’s lead investigator on the Kony case, about the group's resurgence.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia and Eritrea break diplomatic ties over conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb8d6e748054cefc1e97da115c300e055b70526b679546bce320082b32e383ef</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T20:28:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-and-eritrea-break-diplomatic-ties-over-conflict--12a4e73260b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-and-eritrea-break-diplomatic-ties-over-conflict" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Ethiopia and Eritrea break diplomatic ties, accusing each other of stoking internal conflicts. Also, Nigeria rolls out a digital postcode system for every building. Plus we speak to one of the co-founders of the Rural Women's Assembly as it is recognised for its work challenging power systems.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian AI expert, Timnit Gebru, wins 'alternative Nobel'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c44c748d249790090529d2cedc0c997f4f9143cd0a99b2dd2acdabc969185f0</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T20:44:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-ai-expert-timnit-gebru-wins-alternative-nobel--fc9f29a4fc4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-ai-expert-timnit-gebru-wins-alternative-nobel" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Africa's richest man breaks ground on a $16 billion oil refinery in Kenya. Also, at universities across Cameroon, programming is overshadowed with uncertainty amidst an indefinite strike by lecturers. Plus we speak to Ethiopian-born computer scientist and pioneering AI ethicist Timnit Gebru as she is honoured with the Swedish Right Livelihood Award for her work on how AI is influenced by biases.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia back to civil war? Horn of Africa fears spillover effect of renewed fighting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a31c5217dd9c6c803bdb023b09d6fbd917fbe5258282ce7ec65a8c6094ef3d9</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:04:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260930-ethiopia-back-to-civil-war-horn-of-africa-fears-spillover-effect-of-renewed-fighting--2f65ee3843c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260930-ethiopia-back-to-civil-war-horn-of-africa-fears-spillover-effect-of-renewed-fighting" /><summary type="html">After contagion in the Arabian Peninsula, should the entire Horn of Africa fear a domino effect? Just as US President Donald Trump’s decision to invade Iran drew the Saudis back to Yemen, did threats over the Bab al-Mandab Strait light the fuse in Ethiopia, where last week, unresolved issues between the government and its Tigray region erupted? Could a potential return to civil war draw in regional rivals?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's last Jews dream of visa for Israel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85a9515402ad375bdee824a501683a5062fc84afbd5d020aea82536053340dc7</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:55:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260930-ethiopia-s-last-jews-dream-of-visa-for-israel--0983188429c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260930-ethiopia-s-last-jews-dream-of-visa-for-israel" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia has one of the oldest Jewish communities in the world, rumoured to be the descendants of the Queen of Sheba and King Solomon in 950 BC. From the 1970s to 1990s, this community known as Beta Israel was persecuted under the Communist regime, and Israel evacuated more than 20,000 Ethiopian Jews in dramatic airlifts known as Operation Solomon and Operation Moses. But a few thousand were left behind.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry></feed>
